# `dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome`

The result of a black-box mesh-adaptive run.

`minimizer` is the best point; `objective_vector` holds its objective values (several for a multi-objective problem) and `scalarized_minimum` the single value that was minimised. `status` is a [`BlackboxSolverStatus`](BlackboxSolverStatus.md), `diagnostics` a [`BlackboxAdvancedDiagnostics`](BlackboxAdvancedDiagnostics.md), and `pareto_points` / `pareto_objectives` hold the archive of non-dominated points, one per row.

## Fields

### `minimizer`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

The best point.

### `objective_vector`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

Objective values at the best point.

### `scalarized_minimum`

`double`, default `0`.

The single value minimised.

### `status`

`dfo::BlackboxSolverStatus`, default `ReachedIterationBudget`.

Why the run stopped.

### `diagnostics`

`dfo::BlackboxAdvancedDiagnostics`, default `{}`.

Counters.

### `pareto_points`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

Non-dominated points, one per row.

### `pareto_objectives`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

Their objective vectors, one per row.

## Guidance

Returned by the black-box mesh-adaptive minimizers.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

A single objective.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto black_box = [](const Series &x) {
    dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
    e.objectives = (x - 3.0).square().sum().reshape({1});   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)
    return e;
  };

  const dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome o = dfo::mads_blackbox_minimizer(black_box, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig{});
  out.writeln("minimizer =", o.minimizer.items<double>(), ", minimum =", o.scalarized_minimum, ", status =", dfo::to_string(o.status));
}
```

### Example 2

Two objectives. The objective vector holds both values at the minimizer, and the archive holds the trade-offs found.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(3));
  const auto black_box = [](const Series &x) {
    dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
    const Series a = x.select(0, 0);
    e.objectives = a.square().reshape({1}).unite({(a - 2.0).square().reshape({1})}, 0);
    return e;
  };
  dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig config;
  config.objective_weights = pluss::series::make({0.5, 0.5});
  config.max_evaluations = 600;
  const dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome o = dfo::mads_blackbox_minimizer(black_box, pluss::series::make({5.0}), config);
  out.writeln("x =", o.minimizer.items<double>(), ", objectives =", o.objective_vector.items<double>(), ", archive size =", o.pareto_points.size(0));
}
```

### Example 3

The archive. Every archived point is non-dominated: improving one objective costs the other.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(3));
  const auto black_box = [](const Series &x) {
    dfo::BlackboxEvaluation e;
    const Series a = x.select(0, 0);
    e.objectives = a.square().reshape({1}).unite({(a - 2.0).square().reshape({1})}, 0);
    return e;
  };
  dfo::MadsBlackboxAdvancedConfig config;
  config.pareto_archive_limit = 5;
  config.objective_weights = pluss::series::make({0.5, 0.5});
  config.max_evaluations = 600;
  const dfo::BlackboxAdvancedOutcome o = dfo::mads_blackbox_minimizer(black_box, pluss::series::make({5.0}), config);
  out.writeln("points  =", o.pareto_points.reshape({o.pareto_points.numel()}).items<double>());
}
```

